{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1277009,"num_turns":128,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"30044a02-e4bd-47a4-a681-7bf3ddb59184","total_cost_usd":14.686150000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":230665,"cache_read_input_tokens":20014968,"output_tokens":94684,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":230665,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1165,"cache_read_input_tokens":249891,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3721,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0038009999999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":223,"outputTokens":94684,"cacheReadInputTokens":20014968,"cacheCreationInputTokens":230665,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":14.682349000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The full test suite is running against the final tree; I'll continue when it reports. Meanwhile, here's where cycle 4 stands.\n\n**The cycle-3 P1, closed on both halves:**\n\n1. **`Publish` compensates its own mutations.** `internal/buildcache/publish.go:182-198` arms the compensation before the selection loop can move anything, tracking the two live mutations (`displaced`, `selected`). Every exit — quarantine failure, conflict, lost lock, winner-validation failure, cache-root sync failure, and the exhausted retry loop — unwinds exactly what happened. The contract is now stated on the method and on `CachePublisher`: an error from `Publish` means the cache root is what `Publish` found, so the commit phase records nothing to revert for it.\n\n2. **`Revert` is fail-closed and shares that implementation** (`restoreDisplaced`). A restoration that fails puts the withdrawn entry back, so the slot is never left empty with a usable entry sitting in quarantine. Nothing is deleted on any path.\n\n3. **The truth reaches the operator.** `buildcache.StateChangedError` / `StateChanged(err)` marks the cases where the cache really was left changed. `runCommit` maps all three retention causes — in-flight journal, publication that couldn't compensate, reversal that didn't complete — to `BuildCacheRetained`, each with its own warning. The repair notice stopped naming a single cause it can't know.\n\n**Fault seams and coverage** — one unexported hook on `Store`, never set by `New`, at all seven boundaries the verdict named (quarantine, selection/exhaustion, validation, sync, withdrawal, restore, reversal sync). The cases assert byte-identical live entries, unchanged live-entry counts, a quarantine count that never shrinks, no surviving staging directory, and that a failed compensation never leaves the slot empty. The selection fault stands in for the rename rather than short-circuiting, which is what makes the loop-exhaustion exit reachable.\n\n**Install and upgrade** — two new `internal/install` tests for the publication and reversal retention paths (both asserting the whole `snapshotState` map is unchanged), and the real-CLI `TestInstallAndUpgradeRestoreTheCacheWhenTheCommitFails` extended with a full installed-state fingerprint covering launcher bytes, adapter mirrors, runtime, hybrid store, and the consumer ledger — plus a guard so it can't pass by comparing nothing to nothing.\n\nGates so far, real exit codes, run standalone: `gofmt -l cmd internal` → 0 (no output), `go build ./...` → 0, `go vet ./...` → 0, `golangci-lint run ./...` (pinned v2.4.0) → 0, **0 issues**, `go test ./internal/buildcache` → 0, `go test ./internal/install/...` → 0, and the install+upgrade E2E → 0. The repository-wide `go test ./...` is the one still in flight; I restarted it twice so the log matches the final tree rather than a mid-edit snapshot, and the earlier two runs are non-evidence.","ttft_ms":2906,"ttft_stream_ms":1866,"time_to_request_ms":31,"type":"result","duration_ms":1885958,"uuid":"7e9537c9-eb26-4a90-b1d0-96e0d949d8a3"}
